    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="327" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Mixing a concentrate Sam bought a large bottle of concentrated cleaning solution at the warehouse store. He must mix the concentrate with water to make a solution for washing his windows. The directions tell him to mix $$3$$ ounces of concentrate with $$5$$ ounces of water. If he puts $$12$$ ounces of concentrate in a bucket, how many ounces of water should he add? How many ounces of the solution will he have altogether?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>He must add 20 oz of water to obtain a final solution of 32 oz.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="328" has_solution="false">
